<!--
     Face unlock VINTF declaration.

     This REPLACES the extracted blob vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/face-default_3.xml,
     which is dropped from proprietary-files.txt. Two reasons:

     1. THE BLOB IN THE VENDOR TREE HAD BEEN HAND-EDITED TO version 4. Stock's copy
        says 3, and the vendor blob tree is not under version control, so that edit
        was untracked and would vanish on the next extract. Shipping our own file
        makes it reproducible and reviewable.

     2. VERSION 4 WAS WRONG. The implementation is V3:

          $ readelf -dW android.hardware.biometrics.face-service.face-isv | grep NEEDED
            android.hardware.biometrics.face-V3-ndk.so
            android.hardware.biometrics.common-V3-ndk.so

        This is the same shape as the wifi HAL bug. A blob declared at a version it
        does not implement registers cleanly and then aborts inside the newer NDK
        backend on the first real transaction. Declare what the binary serves.

        Nothing forced the bump either: AOSP's own framework compatibility matrix
        (hardware/interfaces/compatibility_matrices/compatibility_matrix.202404.xml
        and .202504.xml) accepts version 3-4 for this HAL.

     DECLARING THIS HAL IS ONLY SAFE ALONGSIDE THE SEPOLICY THAT LETS IT START,
     and alongside the feature XML. While the binary was labelled vendor_file init
     could not exec it:

       init: Could not ctl.start for 'biometrics-face-hal': File
             /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.biometrics.face-service.face-isv
             (labeled "u:object_r:vendor_file:s0") has incorrect label or no
             domain transition from u:r:init:s0

     That did not hang anything, because SystemServer only builds FaceService when
     the android.hardware.biometrics.face feature is declared, and it was not. The
     three pieces together are safe; the feature XML on its own would recreate the
     declared-but-absent stall that hit weaver and fingerprint earlier in this port.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.biometrics.face</name>
        <version>3</version>
        <fqname>IFace/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
